# AWS DynamoDB Provisioning with Terraform

## 📌 Project Overview
This repository contains the Terraform configuration used to provision an Amazon DynamoDB table for storing user data as part of the Nautilus DevOps infrastructure tasks.

---

## 📋 Task Specifications
* **Table Name:** `datacenter-users`
* **Primary Key (Partition Key):** `datacenter_id` (Type: `String`)
* **Billing Mode:** `PAY_PER_REQUEST` (On-Demand)
* **Working Directory:** `/home/bob/terraform`
* **Configuration File:** `main.tf`

---

## 🛠️ Infrastructure Configuration (`main.tf`)

```hcl
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "datacenter_users" {
  name         = "datacenter-users"
  billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key     = "datacenter_id"

  attribute {
    name = "datacenter_id"
    type = "S"
  }
}


Execution & Deployment Steps
Navigate to Working Directory:
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform apply -auto-approve

